WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.750
A duke sits buried in his books.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.300
"Me, poor man, my library
was dukedom large enough."

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.390
Behind him, his brother
quietly lifts the coronet away.

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.510
Twelve years later, on an island,
he raises a storm with one gesture.

5
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.070
A spirit, a servant and a young
prince all move when he points.

6
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.850
When the spirit complains, he
warns: "If thou more murmur'st,

7
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.810
I will rend an oak".

8
00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.080
He was robbed.

9
00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:30.740
But has he become a tyrant himself?

10
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.250
In this mission, you'll hear
how Prospero lost Milan,

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.550
and ask whether he had a hand in it.

12
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.180
You'll weigh how he treats
Ariel, Caliban and Ferdinand,

13
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.210
and see why readers
judge him so differently.

14
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.660
Your mission: decide whether
Prospero is a victim or a tyrant.
